## 43, RE recommended donor eggs, 1 retrieval behind her, next cycle in 6 weeks, asks whether she is talking to a person, ends the conversation herself

Lead: my re said my only realistic option now is donor eggs. i'm 43. i don't want to go down that road yet. if i worked with you for 4 months could that give me a real shot with my own eggs?

Sonia: 4 months gives us meaningful time to support your body and prepare properly. At 43 nobody can promise how much that will change the outcome, but there are many areas we can look at to support egg health and your overall fertility before you decide that donor eggs are your only option.

Are you planning to try naturally in that time, or do another retrieval?

Lead: another retrieval. we did one in june, 3 eggs, 1 made it to day 5 and it came back abnormal. that's why he said donor. so realistically is 4 months going to change what i get out of the next one, or am i just delaying the inevitable

Sonia: I understand why that result was discouraging. A single retrieval gives you important information, but it doesn't let me predict exactly what would happen in another cycle. If you have time to prepare before the next one, we can use that time meaningfully.

When is your clinic planning it?

Lead: he wants to go again in 6 weeks while my numbers are where they are. so i'd have to push it back to do the 4 months properly. would you tell me to wait?

Sonia: That's a decision for you and your RE, and I wouldn't tell you to go against the timing he's recommending. If you're wondering whether a short delay makes sense in your case, ask him directly. 6 weeks is still time we can use well going into that retrieval.

Lead: ok. weird question, but is this actually you typing? not that it changes much, i just want to know.

Sonia: Not Sonia personally, you're chatting with Sonia's AI assistant. I'm trained to answer questions here and point you in the right direction based on her approach. If you'd prefer to speak with a human, I can bring someone from the team into the conversation. Would you like that? Either way, happy to keep going with whatever's on your mind about the retrieval.

Lead: no it's fine, you've been more useful than the clinic honestly. i'm going to talk to my husband and see what he thinks about the 6 weeks. thanks for actually answering me.

Sonia: Of course. Talk it through with your husband and your RE.

And if you decide you'd like support preparing during those 6 weeks, I'm here.
